---
title: "4 · Completed documents and evidence"
description: Confirm the completion date, download the signed PDF, resend the completion notice, and see how each signature was given.
sidebar:
  order: 5
  label: "4 · Completed documents and evidence"
---

**Who:** the sender or a tenant admin. **Where:** the request's page.

## Confirm the completion date

A request with a completion date field (**+ Date**) does not complete on its own. When everyone has signed, it becomes **Awaiting date**, and the sender is told. The date printed on the document is the one the sender confirms.

{% steps %}

1. Open the request. On **By document**, select **Confirm completion date** on the document.
2. Check the signed document in the preview. The **Completion date** is filled in with Operon's suggestion, the date of the last signature; change it if needed.
3. Select **Confirm and complete**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="e-sign/detail-confirm-date" caption="Confirming the completion date before the request completes." /%}

Only the sender and a tenant admin can confirm the date; anyone else sees that the date is waiting to be confirmed. A request without a date field becomes **Completed** as soon as the last signer signs.

## When the request is completed

- The signed PDF is stamped with every signature (and the completion date) and kept with the request. Select **Download** on the document's row to save it.
- Signers are emailed when every party has signed and can download the final documents from their link for 90 days.
- CC recipients get a download link.

To send the signers the signed documents again, select **Resend completion notice** on the **Collect signed documents** card and confirm. The card says how many people it was sent to.

{% screenshot id="e-sign/detail-completed" caption="A completed request: the signed document can be downloaded and the completion notice resent." /%}

## Evidence of signing

Operon keeps, for each signer, what is needed to show how the document was signed:

- **How and when** — point at a signer on **By document** to see the signature method (**Drawn**, **Typed**, **Uploaded**, **Saved signature** or **Signed by the platform**) and the time of signing.
- **Signature pages seen** — the time each signature page was shown to the signer on screen. "Sign all" can be used only after every signature page has been seen.
- **How the signature was confirmed** — place by place, with "Sign all", or, for agreements signed when a firm joins Operon, by a single confirmation.
- **Every email** — the **Sent emails** list on the **Emails** card keeps each invitation, reminder and notice exactly as sent, with its delivery state.

For a case signing step where some signers signed on paper, **Download merged** on the case's signing card puts the e-signed copy and the paper copies into one PDF with a **Signing Record** page: who signed which document, how (online or on paper, with the confirmation method and the signature pages seen) and when (SGT).

The signed PDFs, the signing record and the dates are always in English, whatever the language of the interface.
